`display: contents` does not prevent an element’s pseudo-elements from generating boxes. The element itself generates no box, but its children and pseudo-elements still generate boxes as normal, as if they had replaced the element in the box tree. ([CSS Display Module Level 3](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-display/))

However, `::before` and `::after` generate boxes only when their computed `content` value is not `none`. ([CSS Pseudo-Elements Module Level 4](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-pseudo))

```css
.parent {
  display: contents;
}

.parent::before {
  content: "Generated content";
}
```

If `content` is omitted or computes to `none`, the pseudo-element is not generated.
